Good. This is actually the correct time to do cleanup work.

If you jump directly into the new architecture, you'll end up debugging:

```text
old bugs
+ subprocess bugs
+ concurrency bugs
+ browser isolation bugs
```

all at once.

I'd create a stabilization phase first.

# Name of the Architecture

I would call it:

```text
Hermes Cell Architecture (HCA)
```

because each application runs inside an isolated execution cell.

```text
Hermes Parent
   ├─ Cell A
   ├─ Cell B
   └─ Cell C (future)
```

Alternative names:

```text
Hermes Execution Cells (HEC)
Hermes Isolated Worker Cells (HIWC)
Hermes Application Cell Runtime (ACR)
```

My vote:

**Hermes Cell Architecture (HCA)**

---

# Stage 0 — Stabilization Before HCA

This is what I'd do before touching architecture.

---

## Priority 1

### Fix the repeated timeout accumulation

This is the most important thing in the entire system.

Current suspicion:

```text
30 sec timeout
→ exception swallowed

30 sec timeout
→ exception swallowed

30 sec timeout
→ exception swallowed

45 times later
→ 24 minutes gone
```

You need exact proof.

Goal:

```text
Find:
- exact loop
- exact exception
- exact retry path
- exact state machine path
```

before architecture work.

---

## Priority 2

### Introduce Failure Taxonomy

Right now too many things become:

```text
FAILED
```

You need:

```text
FAILED_TIMEOUT
FAILED_BROWSER
FAILED_CAPTCHA
FAILED_FORM_LOOP
FAILED_UPLOAD
FAILED_NAVIGATION
FAILED_PLATFORM
FAILED_UNKNOWN
```

Why?

Because after subprocesses arrive:

```text
child died
```

must become:

```text
WHY did child die?
```

otherwise debugging becomes impossible.

---

## Priority 3

### Browser Ownership Cleanup

Currently browser ownership looks fuzzy.

Need:

```text
Application
↓
Browser PID
↓
Profile
↓
Xvfb
↓
Screenshot Folder
```

stored together.

Every browser should have:

```text
session_id
job_id
browser_pid
profile_path
xvfb_display
```

attached.

This makes future cell isolation much easier.

---

## Priority 4

### Profile Isolation

Today:

```text
single browser
single profile
```

Future:

```text
Browser A → Profile A

Browser B → Profile B
```

Prepare this now.

Create profile abstraction before concurrency exists.

Example:

```python
profile_manager.acquire()
profile_manager.release()
```

Even if only one profile exists today.

---

## Priority 5

### Remove Global State

Subprocess architectures hate globals.

Audit:

```text
globals
singletons
module caches
shared temp files
fixed paths
fixed screenshots
```

Look for:

```python
/tmp/hermes
/tmp/chrome
output/latest.png
```

stuff.

Anything shared becomes a future race condition.

---

## Priority 6

### Add Application Phase Tracking

This is huge.

Every application should report:

```text
PHASE_CLAIMED

PHASE_BROWSER_STARTED

PHASE_FORM_FILLING

PHASE_UPLOAD

PHASE_PRE_SUBMIT

PHASE_SUBMIT_INTENT

PHASE_SUBMITTED

PHASE_COMPLETE
```

Why?

Future parent process needs visibility.

Without this:

```text
child killed
```

means nothing.

With phases:

```text
child killed during upload
```

or

```text
child killed after submit intent
```

Huge difference.

---

## Priority 7

### Screenshot Discipline

Today screenshots seem incidental.

Make them deterministic.

For every failure:

```text
before timeout

before kill

before retry

before browser cleanup
```

capture evidence.

Later this becomes critical.

---

## Priority 8

### Introduce Structured Events

Instead of:

```python
logger.info("clicked continue")
```

move toward:

```python
event(
    type="button_click",
    job_id=2110,
    page="application",
    button="continue"
)
```

This will massively help debugging cells.

---

## Priority 9

### Retry Policy Cleanup

Currently retries appear mixed together.

Need explicit policy:

```text
Timeout → retry

Captcha → retry later

Platform rejection → no retry

Already applied → no retry

Browser crash → retry
```

before subprocesses arrive.

---

## Priority 10

### Measure True Throughput

Before architecture changes establish:

```text
Applications/hour

Success rate

Average runtime

P95 runtime

P99 runtime

Timeout count

Browser crash count
```

otherwise you won't know if HCA actually helped.

---

# Then Build HCA

Only after those 10 items.

Then:

```text
Phase 1
---------
Fix timeout accumulation

Phase 2
---------
Failure taxonomy
+
phase tracking

Phase 3
---------
Browser/profile isolation

Phase 4
---------
Hermes Cell Architecture

Parent
  ├ Cell A
  └ Cell B

Phase 5
---------
Measure

Phase 6
---------
Increase to 3 cells if justified
```

If you do the above, the architecture migration becomes dramatically easier because you're converting a well-observed system into isolated cells rather than trying to isolate a black box.
